  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: netty-codec-redis 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released io.netty:netty-codec-redis 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-42586, CVE-2026-44250, CVE-2026-44890, CVE-2026-48006, CVE-2026-50011, and CVE-2026-56818.\n\nCVE-2026-42586: Netty: CRLF Injection in Netty Redis Codec Encoder\n\nCVE-2026-44250: Netty: Memory Exhaustion in RedisArrayAggregator due to Deeply Nested Arrays\n\nCVE-2026-44890: Netty has Unbounded Direct Memory Consumption in its RedisDecoder\n\nCVE-2026-48006: Netty's Lack of Lifecycle Cleanup Leads to Pooled ByteBuf Leak in RedisArrayAggregator\n\nCVE-2026-50011: Netty has unbounded pre-allocation in RedisArrayAggregator from RESP array length\n\nCVE-2026-56818: Netty: RedisArrayAggregator max-elements failure leaves retained partial aggregate state\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for io.netty:netty-codec-redis 4.1.100.Final from Maven Central.",
